  "sortOrder": 55004,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "2 Tim",
    "2Tim",
    "2 Ti",
    "2Ti"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I charge thee therefore before God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, who shall judge the quick and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Preach the word; be instant in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort with all longsuffering and doctrine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts shall they heap to themselves teachers, having itching ears;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And they shall turn away their ears from the truth, and shall be turned unto fables.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But watch thou in all things, endure afflictions, do the work of an evangelist, make full proof of thy ministry.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Do thy diligence to come shortly unto me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For Demas hath forsaken me, having loved this present world, and is departed unto Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus unto Dalmatia.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Only Luke is with me. Take Mark, and bring him with thee: for he is profitable to me for the ministry.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And Tychicus have I sent to Ephesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The cloke that I left at Troas with Carpus, when thou comest, bring with thee, and the books, but especially the parchments.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Alexander the coppersmith did me much evil: the Lord reward him according to his works:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Of whom be thou ware also; for he hath greatly withstood our words.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "At my first answer no man stood with me, but all men forsook me: I pray God that it may not be laid to their charge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Notwithstanding the Lord stood with me, and strengthened me; that by me the preaching might be fully known, and that all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And the Lord shall deliver me from every evil work, and will preserve me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the household of Onesiphorus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Erastus abode at Corinth: but Trophimus have I left at Miletum sick.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Do thy diligence to come before winter. Eubulus greeteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:2-timothy:4:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The Lord Jesus Christ be with thy spirit. Grace be with you. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "2 Timothy 4:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:2-timothy:4:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
